<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, hey!”</span> She says without even turning around, so focused on shooting down the banditos. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thanks. Not my best game, but I’d say I’m pretty alright.”</span> You laugh, claiming she is more than pretty alright. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“You should see me in the paintball game we have on our Woo at home. Hey, want to join next game?”</span> <br>
<br>
Though a little intimidated by her skill, you agree and take the seat next to her. It doesn’t take her long to finish the level and reset for another round. You scoff as she offers to lower the difficulty, though the <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nightmare”</span> difficulty setting she’s playing on does spook you a little. Then, as the game begins, you ready your pistol! <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightGreen"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lea</span> ’s skill is even more impressive when you have to fight alongside her. She is constantly clearing her side as you fumble and panic as the number of bandits increases. Thankfully, she provides help when you need it and is able to help keep you alive. She also doesn’t mock or tease your skill, instead being very encouraging. You suspect this is how she treats her twin brother.</span> <br>
<br>
Right as the level is ramping up, you get a strange feeling. A feeling of being watched. You glance briefly to your right between waves, since you only have a second before you have to get blasting again, <span style="Color: Yellow">and see an employee of the arcade standing right behind you both. You suddenly feel your body stiffen and become far too aware of every awkward movement you make. The round seems to last forever as you feel their eyes piercing your back. Then, once it finally ends, you nearly jump as you feel a hand on your shoulder.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Sorry, we need to take this extra chair. We have someone who can’t stand for very long at one of the other games.”</span> He explains as he nearly yanks the chair out from under you. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Your girlfriend can keep hers though.”</span> You blush, <span style="Color: Pink">trying to panickly explain that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lea</span> is just a friend, but the employee doesn’t say anything as he takes the chair and leaves.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Hahaha,”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lea</span>  laughs, both at the employee’s inference and your reaction, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Don’t worry, boyfriend,”</span> She teases with a smirk, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“you can have my chair. I’ve been sitting for a while so should stretch my legs anyway. Now come on, we still have a few more rounds!”</span> <br>
<br>

